    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/4/64559.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 4,
    "turn_text": "You know, Tim, to sit there and listen to a man who says one thing and does another is unfair to the American people. This is the State of the Union is a time for President layout, his visions, his goals, uplifting message. And as I was sitting there, the man is not in reality. He keeps saying these things. And as an example, when he said, fund the police, he agrees with that. He's got a vice president that put up bond money to get criminals out of jail. When he said, treatment, mental and mental treatment, health, uh, options for those, uh, with drug overdoses across the borders coming to loads of fentanyl and cocaine in marijuana. When he mentioned securing the border, uh, build the wall. I mean, is it that complicated? And then what, uh, what got me is when he said he wanted to bring manufacturing back to the United States, you don't do it by raising taxes and putting dis incentives and putting regulations on. So it was a disconnected speech. It was one that was what I expected, but I was hoping better. He did try to shift to the middle, but what came across loud and clear to me is he is totally driven by the left, the socialist Democrat wing of the party, which is pretty much all the Democrats now. And he thinks we're stupid enough, the American people are stupid enough to buy his words. Oh, after a year and four months, nobody's buying his words. That's why his ratings are so low. And he thinks he can make a talk in March 2nd. and change Americans' minds. I don't think it's gonna work.",
