  {
    "episode_id": 64559,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/4/64559.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "And Tim, he's the one that talks about bipartisanship. When he ran, he was going to be the great Uniner. How is that uniting anybody? All of his junk legislation from the infrastructure bill to the so-called voter rights bill to the women's health. I mean, it's all a rouge. And they bulldozed these bills through. And it's been no partisanship. We can't offer amendments. There's no cuts. He's good at spending our money. But there they he believes that government is is should run everything. And he's a socialist and he sold out. I mean, you can't make this many mistakes as he has made that affect the country like it's affected me.",
