  {
    "episode_id": 64559,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/4/64559.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "Where's where's the logic in this? There is no logic. It's a control factor. That's why we wrote Mayor Bowser and said, what are you doing? Why are you still mandating masks for teachers and for children? Children's are the least affected. Children, the infection rate is down 80% in Washington. The COVID cases are down nationwide. And it doesn't affect children that much anyway. And if you want to have social distancing, that's one thing. But Tim, I think it's a control factor. They just want to keep it going. And, you know, when she, you know, imagine shut the businesses down and a disallowing customers to come in unless you've had a shot in your arm. It shows you this administration is willing to take for a person to if they don't take the shot, which is a personal freedom. It's a 10th Amendment state's rights issue anyway. But to do that and to deny food on the table that he's did to tell the military that defend this country that if they don't put a substance in their body they can't serve. I mean, they will go to no end to accomplish their power struggle or get control.",
